* ==================================================================
* tb_timing_budget_closure -- issue #12's conversion timing budget,
* composed from #8/#9/#10's real worst-case numbers instead of
* spec/prior-art-survey.md Sec 1.4's placeholder DAC model, at both
* the 1 MS/s target (r1, 62.5 ns bit cycle) and the 2 MS/s stretch
* (r2, 31.25 ns bit cycle).
*
* GENERATED by design/sar-logic/gen_sar_logic.py -- do not edit.
*
* Per rate, four single-ended loops, identical except for the
* candidate logic-propagation delay added on top of the FIXED,
* measured 863 ps comparator regeneration delay (#9):
*   l0    +0 ns    just the two closed, measured/derived terms
*   l10   +10 ns   a generous logic-delay allowance -- still well
*                  inside both rates' margin per
*                  spec/timing-budget-memo.md
*   l25   +25 ns   inside the 1 MS/s margin (~52 ns) but OVER the
*                  2 MS/s stretch margin (~21 ns) -- the illustrative
*                  case the memo reports: the stretch's margin can
*                  go negative before the target's does
*   l55   +55 ns   over BOTH rates' margin -- the negative control
*
* Same PVT-subset justification as sim/sar-logic-timing/: rung-1
* ideal-digital + behavioural analog carries no PDK device models, so
* process/temperature cannot move anything here. The worst-PVT-corner
* claim is carried by the injected component VALUES (R_WORST_BIT_OHM,
* C_WORST_BIT_F, T_COMP_REGEN_NS above), each sourced from a closed,
* full-grid PVT sweep (#8/#9/#10), not by sweeping this deck's own
* corners.
* ==================================================================

